les. The project is modularized into commands, core utilities, components, and schemas, enabling clear separation of concerns and facilitating future extensions.\",\n  \"observationsAndLimitations\": [\n    \"The commit only adds files; no functional tests or CI configuration are present.\",\n    \"The AI engine script relies on an NVIDIA API key hard‑coded in .env.example, which may not be secure for production.\",\n    \"The bun.lock file is extremely large, potentially impacting install times.\",\n    \"The project includes both Node.js and Python components but does not provide a unified build or deployment pipeline.\",\n    \"No error handling for missing dependencies or environment variables is included in the CLI commands.\",\n    \"The React UI references assets that may not be present in the repository root.\",\n    \"The commit does not include any documentation for the API endpoints used by the AI engine.\",\n    \"The TypeScript configuration uses experimental decorators without corresponding code.\",\n    \"The project relies on a specific version of the NVIDIA model (meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct) but does not provide fallback logic.\"\n  ],\n  \"confidenceScore\": 0.95,\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-oss-20b\",\n  \"processingTimeMs\": 150596\n}"
